{"repositoryId":1423156946,"availability":"available","full":"KarinaKKarinaK/imperial-hackathon","name":"imperial-hackathon","description":"Explore this public GitHub project.","category":"Other","language":"JavaScript","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-10-17T09:27:21Z","updated":"2026-10-19T15:47:34Z","branch":"main","homepage":"https://metricsfile.vercel.app","topics":[],"demo":"https://metricsfile.vercel.app/","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-19T15:56:13.043Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-19T15:56:13.043Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-19T15:56:13.043Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-19T15:56:13.043Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Imperial Global Hackathon Hong Kong and Macau 2026, University track, Challenge 6 (open challenge).","Hong Kong's 2026 Policy Address (para 385) promises statutory injury compensation for delivery platform workers. Platforms will carry the liability. Nobody has objective data on when and how riders get hurt, so claims cannot be verified and risk cannot be priced. A 2024 union survey found only 13% of injured riders were compensated.","We are building a verified work-injury event record: a low-cost helmet sensor and phone app that detect crashes and flag fatigue and heat risk, a triage alert for dispatchers, and a parametric micro-insurance trigger that pays out on a verified event. We are the sensor, the trigger and the data standard. We are not the insurer."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/KarinaKKarinaK/imperial-hackathon/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"23633031977617a6bd60ca64a117aaf6586fd68735a4a5004761c3094b5838a3","extractedAt":"2026-10-19T15:56:13.197Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-19T15:56:13.197Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Imperial Global Hackathon Hong Kong and Macau 2026, University track, Challenge 6 (open challenge).","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/KarinaKKarinaK/imperial-hackathon/blob/main/READM